      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(infra): deduplicate pricing fingerprint in usage-cost cache",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe per-agent usage-cost cache stores the full `pricingFingerprint` string (~2.7 KB) on every entry. The fingerprint is identical across all entries, so on large caches it dominates the file — ~57% of a 142 MB cache as pure duplication.\n\nCloses #99511\n\n## Root Cause / Fix\n\nEvery `UsageCostCacheFileEntry` carried a copy of the same `pricingFingerprint` string. The fix stores it once at the `UsageCostCacheFile` level and strips it from entries before serialization. On load, `normalizeUsageCostCache` transparently restores the fingerprint to entries from the file level, so all internal code reading `entry.pricingFingerprint` is unchanged. The active fingerprint is persisted before every cache write in `refreshCostUsageCacheForPath`.\n\n**+6 lines changed. No internal references touched.**\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real production function proof (cold cache round-trip)\n\nCreated two session transcript files, ran `refreshCostUsageCache()`, then inspected the serialized cache file:\n\n```text\n=== Real cache file proof (#99511) ===\nFile level pricingFingerprint: PRESENT ✅\n  length: 113 bytes\nEntries with pricingFingerprint: 0/2 ✅\nEntries total: 2\nFile size: 1,593 bytes\n```\n\nThe fingerprint is stored once at the file level; entries are stripped.\n\n### Pricing-change round-trip\n\nExisting test `invalidates durable aggregate cache when gateway pricing cache changes` verifies that changing the pricing config correctly invalidates the cache. Setting the active fingerprint before each write ensures the cache is rebuilt when the pricing model changes.\n\n### Before/after serialization comparison\n\n```text\nBefore: { version: 4, files: { \"a.jsonl\": { ..., pricingFingerprint: \"sha256:abc...\", ... }, \"b.jsonl\": { ..., pricingFingerprint: \"sha256:abc...\", ... } } }\n            ↑ duplicated on every entry\n\nAfter:  { version: 4, pricingFingerprint: \"sha256:abc...\", files: { \"a.jsonl\": { ... }, \"b.jsonl\": { ... } } }\n            ↑ stored once at file level\n```\n\n## Change Type\n- [x] Performance fix\n## Scope\n- [x] Infrastructure (usage-cost cache)\n## Security Impact\n- New permissions? No · Secrets changed? No · New network calls? No\n",
